\par\par \uc2 Technology & Media\par \b \uc2 Visa\uc2  Plans Layoffs as Part Of International Revamp --- About 1,000 cuts are expected to eliminate positions in technology area\b0\par\par\uc2 By Angel Au-Yeung \par \uc2 343 \uc2 words\par \uc2 30 October 2024\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B4\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Visa\uc2  plans to lay off around 1,400 employees and contractors by the end of the year, according to people familiar with the matter, as part of a plan to streamline its international business.\par \par \uc2 Employees learned in an internal announcement last week that the company planned to cut jobs, though exact details weren't provided, the people said.\par \par \uc2 Roughly 1,000 of the cuts are expected to eliminate technology positions, while most of the rest will focus on merchant sales and global digital partnerships roles, they said. The latter team manages the company's relationships with fintech and tech companies such as \uc2 Amazon\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Visa\uc2  has over 30,000 employees worldwide. Some of the cuts will be of contractors on its engineering teams. It couldn't be learned how many of those affected aren't employees.\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 Visa\uc2  spokesman said the company continuously evolves to better serve clients and support growth, "which can lead to the elimination of some roles." He said the company expects to employ more people each year for the foreseeable future.\par \par \uc2 Some of the layoffs occurred last week. For workers in the global digital partnership teams, \uc2 Visa\uc2  plans to keep them employed through the end of the year, the people said. It is also encouraging those affected to apply for open positions.\par \par \uc2 Visa\uc2  has been under scrutiny from regulators and dissatisfied merchants and is facing legal challenges from multiple angles.\par \par \uc2 Last month, the Justice Department filed an antitrust lawsuit against \uc2 Visa\uc2 , alleging it illegally monopolized the market for debit-card payments. \uc2 Visa\uc2  also tried and failed to settle a long-running lawsuit from merchants over the fees they pay to accept credit cards.\par \par \uc2 The company has said it is pro-competition and supports innovation and commerce.\par \par \uc2 Visa\uc2  reported its fourth-quarter earnings Tuesday afternoon, showing a 12% jump in revenue and a 14% jump in net income.\par \par \uc2 Payments volume rose 8% from a year ago.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020241030ekau0001u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
