\par\par \b \uc2 Boeing Union Rejects Pact, Extending Strike\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sharon Terlep \par \uc2 581 \uc2 words\par \uc2 24 October 2024\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par A1\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2 's largest union rejected a new labor deal Wednesday, extending a six-week strike that has plunged the jet maker into increasing financial peril.\par \par \uc2 Members of the machinist union voted 64% against a proposed contact that would have delivered a 35% wage increase over four years, union leaders said.\par \par \uc2 Without a deal, factories that build the 737, 767 and 777 jets remain idled, further sapping the company's revenue and risking more disruption in its supply chain.\par \par \uc2 The vote came on the same day \uc2 Boeing\uc2  warned investors that it would burn through cash into 2025 after burning through more than $10 billion in the first nine months of 2024. Analysts estimate the walkout is costing \uc2 Boeing\uc2  around $1 billion a month.\par \par \uc2 Credit-ratings firms have warned they may downgrade \uc2 Boeing\uc2  into junk status.\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2  declined to comment.\par \par \uc2 The strike by 33,000 members of the \uc2 International Association of Machinists and Aerospace Workers\uc2  has already rippled beyond \uc2 Boeing\uc2  and prompted some suppliers to cut staff or furlough workers. An extended halt in production would further delay aircraft deliveries that airlines need.\par \par \uc2 Jon Holden, president of the local IAM chapter, said members are angry over years of concessions made under the threat of losing jobs. They want to see pensions restored or an alternative beyond the company's offer of increased 401(k) payments, he said. "They haven't gone far enough in other ways to replace it," Holden said.\par \par \uc2 Ending the stoppage is a priority for \uc2 Boeing\uc2  Chief Executive \uc2 Kelly Ortberg\uc2 , who recently set plans to cut 17,000 jobs and sell at least $10 billion in shares to plug the company's cash drain.\par \par \uc2 Before the vote, Ortberg said the company was "feverishly working to find a solution that works for the company and meets our employees' needs."\par \par \uc2 The proposed 35% wage increase was up from \uc2 Boeing\uc2 's original offer of 25%. Both offers were rejected by employees in the Pacific Northwest whose wages haven't kept up with the cost of living in the area. The average wage for a \uc2 Boeing\uc2  machinist was about $75,000 under the prior contract.\par \par \uc2 The revised proposal included a $7,000 ratification bonus and the restoration of annual bonuses that were eliminated in the initial proposal.\par \par \uc2 The latest offer wouldn't have restored pensions, which was a demand of many members, but something union leaders had said might be out of reach. \uc2 Boeing\uc2  would have increased company 401(k) contributions, including a one-time payment of $5,000 to all workers' retirement accounts.\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2  employee Vaughn Johnson voted against the deal, though he said it was a marked improvement from the first offer.\par \par \uc2 "It's the first real offer from the company," he said. Johnson, who is married and has a 2-year-old child, said the contract would have brought worker pay even with inflation since the last contract in 2014 but didn't feel like a substantial raise beyond that. "It sounds good but if you factor in buying power, it still seems like we haven't gotten a real raise."\par \par \uc2 Earlier Wednesday, \uc2 Boeing\uc2  posted a $6.17 billion loss, its biggest quarterly loss since 2020, when the pandemic shut down air travel. The company had warned it would take billions of dollars in charges on troubled projects.\par \par \uc2 The third-quarter results were in line with its warning: a net loss of $9.97 a share on revenue of $17.8 billion.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020241024ekao0000u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
