\par\par \b \uc2 Business News: \uc2 PPG\uc2  Sells Coatings Business, To Cut 1,800 Jobs\b0\par\par\uc2 By Don Nico Forbes \par \uc2 239 \uc2 words\par \uc2 18 October 2024\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 PPG\uc2  said it agreed to sell its architectural-coatings business in the U.S. and Canada to private-equity firm \uc2 American Industrial Partners\uc2  for $550 million, and outlined a cost-reduction program that will affect around 1,800 employees.\par \par \uc2 The paint-and-coatings manufacturer on Thursday said that the sale of the businesses, which represented roughly $2 billion of sales in 2023, is expected to close in late 2024 or early 2025 and is aimed at boosting organic growth.\par \par \uc2 The Pittsburgh company reported total sales of $18.2 billion in 2023.\par \par \uc2 PPG\uc2  added it would implement a cost-reduction program with expected annual pretax savings of about $175 million, including savings of $60 million in 2025.\par \par \uc2 "While these decisions are difficult, they are necessary to adjust our fixed cost base and to right-size our company following these two business divestitures," Chief Executive \uc2 Tim Knavish\uc2  said. "None of these actions will impact our ongoing investments or focus on organic growth."\par \par \uc2 The company said structural costs will primarily be reduced in Europe, and will affect about 1,800 jobs, largely in Europe and the U.S.\par \par \uc2 It had 53,000 employees as of Dec 31, 2023, according to \uc2 FactSet\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The company expects to record a pretax charge of roughly $250 million in the fourth quarter of 2024, with further charges anticipated over the next few years.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020241018ekai0003b\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
