\par\par \b \uc2 Talks Between \uc2 Boeing\uc2  and Union Break Down\b0\par\par\uc2 By Sharon Terlep \par \uc2 235 \uc2 words\par \uc2 10 October 2024\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B2\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Negotiations broke down between \uc2 Boeing\uc2  and its largest union, eroding hopes of a quick end to a strike that has halted production of most airplanes.\par \par \uc2 Shares fell 3.4% Wednesday.\par \par \uc2 Each side accused the other of refusing to budge late Tuesday. They had resumed talks nearly four weeks into a strike by some 33,000 machinists that build \uc2 Boeing\uc2 's 737 and other planes.\par \par \uc2 "Our team bargained in good faith and made new and improved proposals to try to reach a compromise, including increases in take-home pay and retirement," \uc2 Boeing\uc2  commercial chief \uc2 Stephanie Pope\uc2  said in a note to employees.\par \par \uc2 The union, in a note to members, said \uc2 Boeing\uc2 , after improving its recent offer last month, refused to propose additional increases in wages, retirement contribution and bonuses, among other proposals.\par \par \uc2 "Maybe there's not enough pain to drive both sides to an agreement," Jon Holden, president of the local chapter, said in an interview Tuesday.\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2 's financial picture is increasingly precarious amid the walkout.\par \par \uc2 S&P Global Ratings estimated \uc2 Boeing\uc2  will burn $10 billion in cash this year. It put \uc2 Boeing\uc2  on its CreditWatch negative listing to signal an increased likelihood of a downgrade to "junk" status. All three major credit-rating companies have warned that \uc2 Boeing\uc2  may lose investment-grade status if the strike continues.\par \par \uc2 Boeing\uc2  reports third-quarter financial results Oct. 23.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020241010ekaa00039\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley