\par\par \b \uc2 Business News: Ex-\uc2 Jacksonville Jaguars\uc2  Employee Sues \uc2 FanDuel\uc2  Over Gambling Habit\b0\par\par\uc2 By Katherine Sayre \par \uc2 549 \uc2 words\par \uc2 2 October 2024\par \uc2 The Wall Street Journal\par \uc2 J\par B3\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 Corrections & Amplifications\par \par \uc2 Amit Patel\uc2  is serving a 6 1/2-year federal prison term after pleading guilty to embezzling from the \uc2 Jacksonville Jaguars\uc2  . A Business & Finance article on Wednesday about Patel's lawsuit against \uc2 FanDuel\uc2  incorrectly said he is serving a 6 1/2-month federal prison term.\par \par \uc2 (WSJ Oct. 3, 2024)\par \par \uc2 (END)\par \par \uc2 A former \uc2 Jacksonville Jaguars\uc2  employee who embezzled more than $22 million from the team is suing \uc2 FanDuel\uc2  , alleging that the betting company fueled his fantasy-sports spending and ignored his gambling addiction.\par \par \uc2 Amit Patel\uc2  , who is serving a six-and-a-half-month federal prison term after pleading guilty to stealing money from the team, claimed in a lawsuit filed Tuesday that a \uc2 FanDuel\uc2  VIP host showered him with more than $1 million in betting credits, all-expenses-paid trips and gifts to prey on him. He is seeking $250 million in damages.\par \par \uc2 The gifts ensured that he would "deposit money and gamble in amounts and frequencies that only an addict could ever gamble," the lawsuit says. The lawsuit also claims \uc2 FanDuel\uc2  circumvented anti-money-laundering and other financial rules to keep him depositing more money.\par \par \uc2 A \uc2 FanDuel\uc2  spokesman declined to comment. The lawsuit, which also names \uc2 FanDuel\uc2  parent company \uc2 Flutter Entertainment\uc2  , was filed in federal court in New York.\par \par \uc2 Patel was sentenced earlier this year for stealing from the Jaguars, where he worked on staff and used his role as administrator for the team's virtual credit card program to embezzle the money.\par \par \uc2 Online sports-betting and fantasy-sports companies deploy VIP hosts to build relationships with big-spending customers, monitoring their betting habits and doling out credits and gifts to keep them gambling. Gifts Patel said he received included all-expense-paid trips to the Formula One Grand Prix in Miami and the \uc2 NCAA\uc2  football championship last year.\par \par \uc2 Companies' VIP practices came under federal scrutiny earlier this year. Sen. Richard Blumenthal (D, Conn.) sent letters urging several gambling companies, including \uc2 FanDuel\uc2  , to stop using player data and other marketing tactics to target customers with gambling problems.\par \par \uc2 FanDuel\uc2  knew Patel was a gambling addict based on Patel's deposit amounts and frequency -- a total of more than $20 million through about 1,077 deposits, according to the lawsuit. Patel was diagnosed with a gambling disorder in April 2023, the lawsuit says.\par \par \uc2 In daily fantasy-sports contests, customers build teams of real-life athletes and compete against other teams based on their athletes' performances.\par \par \uc2 Patel's \uc2 FanDuel\uc2  VIP host communicated with him nearly every day between late 2021 and early 2023, through email, phone and text message, the lawsuit alleges.\par \par \uc2 Patel alleges that \uc2 FanDuel\uc2  would give him a $60,000 credit when he reached deposits of at least $600,000 for fantasy sports contests, according to the lawsuit. \uc2 FanDuel\uc2  staff delivered those credits in increments of $25,000, $25,000 and $10,000 to avoid raising suspicions among \uc2 FanDuel\uc2  's internal compliance staff, according to the suit.\par \par \uc2 At one point, the host started communicating with Patel on his personal phone, to avoid detection by \uc2 FanDuel\uc2  's compliance staff and told Patel to fabricate dialogue with the host's \uc2 FanDuel\uc2  phone "to make sure it appears to \uc2 FanDuel\uc2  that their communication remained frequent," the lawsuit alleges.\par \par \uc2 Document J000000020241002eka200006\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw300\pich40\picscaley125\picscalex125\picwgoal3600\pichgoal480
